WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.130
20 April 2010, the Gulf of Mexico.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:09.210
An explosion on the Deepwater Horizon
drilling rig killed 11 workers.

3
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:14.530
Oil poured from a well about
1,520 metres below the surface.

4
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.190
It flowed for 87 days.

5
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.110
About 134 million gallons of oil spilled,

6
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.890
and slicks came ashore
along the Gulf coast.

7
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.870
Yet hotels on a stretch of coast
the oil never reached lost bookings.

8
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.770
So why did they lose bookings?

9
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.510
Did the oil reach them later?

10
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.170
In this mission, you'll
trace the spill's damage,

11
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.850
from the deep water to
marshes, turtles and whales.

12
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.410
Then you'll judge the response, from
booms and dispersants to new rules for the

13
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.470
industry.

14
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.160
Your mission: explain why places
far from the oil still lost out.
